            company: 'Aurum Proptech', rank: 13, stance: 'TURNAROUND', segment: LISTINGS,
            what: "A Mumbai-based property-technology group: co-living and family rentals, developer CRM software (Sell.do), lead generation and PropTiger brokerage, and, since September 2026, Housing.com, bought from REA Group for shares.",
            view: "**A turnaround bet paid for with dilution.** Q2 FY27 revenue rose 64% to ₹130cr, continuing operations made ₹6.8cr before tax (₹1.3cr in Q1), H1 operating cash was ₹60.8cr, and bank debt is gone, with ₹192cr of cash. On 16 Oct 2026 management promised to make Housing.com profitable within 12–18 months. But the H1 headline profit came from selling a building, Housing.com lost about ₹200cr a year, the share count rises about 37% (the deal closed on 29 September 2026, when 1.98cr new shares worth ₹458cr went to REA India, now a 24.9% holder), and management ruled out acquisitions 11 weeks before agreeing this one. Next to CarTrade's profitable classifieds the call stays pass; there is no meaningful P/E to test.",
