    closing: {
        heading: '9. Summary review',
        body: [
            "**Listings and subscriptions.** **Cartrade Tech: own**, the best combination of free traffic, rising margins and cash, though the cash needs a use. **Matrimony.com: follow** for its cash and buybacks, until billing growth returns to double digits and the Jodii rebrand and CFO vacancy settle. **Aurum Proptech: pass**; Housing.com makes it a diluted turnaround, and it is no CarTrade.",
            "**Platforms for businesses.** **BlackBuck: follow**, a strong payments habit, but pre-tax profit must grow again before the price fits. **Macfos: wait** until operating cash turns positive and covers most of its profit (−₹22cr against ₹68cr of profit over five years). **TBO Tek: wait** for the FEMA ruling and a price that fits its organic growth. **Pine Labs: wait** for profit, with the UPI fee as the upside surprise. **Shiprocket: wait** until its newer businesses' losses shrink and the February unlock passes. **Infibeam Avenues (AvenuesAI): pass** while the revenue it keeps shrinks and earnings per share are guided flat. **Turtlemint Fintech: pass** until the insurance regulator's final commission rules show what it can earn.",
            "**Consumer apps.** **Swiggy: wait** for cash break-even and proof that Instamart can hold share. **Urban Company: wait** for InstaHelp's losses to shrink. **One Mobikwik Systems: wait** for profit that does not depend on loan write-backs.",
            "**What would change my view.** For the better: NPCI giving acquirers a solid share of the UPI fee (Pine Labs); Swiggy reaching cash break-even on time; BlackBuck disclosing profitable Superloads hubs; CarTrade announcing a payout; AvenuesAI's net revenue growing again; final insurance commission rules far milder than the draft (Turtlemint); Shiprocket's newer businesses shrinking their losses. For the worse: a new funding wave for quick-commerce rivals; a large FEMA penalty at TBO; Delhivery pricing aggressively against BlackBuck; the truck slowdown arriving harder than ICRA expects; Housing.com's losses not shrinking at Aurum; another regulatory pause at MobiKwik; the insurance caps adopted as drafted (Turtlemint).",
            "**What to watch next quarter.** CarTrade's margin and OLX paid plans; BlackBuck's pre-tax profit; Matrimony.com's billing; Macfos's operating cash; TBO's FEMA case; Swiggy's cash flow and Instamart growth; Urban Company's InstaHelp loss; Pine Labs' contribution margin; MobiKwik's disbursals and write-backs; AvenuesAI's net revenue; Aurum's Housing.com closing and losses; Shiprocket's newer-business loss and contribution margin; Turtlemint's revenue per rupee of premium and the final commission rules.",
        ],
        bottomLine:
            "Own the profitable leader with free traffic and rising margins (Cartrade Tech), follow the good businesses priced ahead of the evidence (BlackBuck, Matrimony.com), wait on the rest until profits, cash and legal cases resolve (Macfos, TBO Tek, Swiggy, Urban Company, Shiprocket, Pine Labs, One Mobikwik Systems), and pass on the payment gateway whose earnings are guided flat (Infibeam Avenues, now AvenuesAI), the insurance broker whose commissions the regulator may cap (Turtlemint Fintech) and the diluted property turnaround (Aurum Proptech).",
    },

